# Attendify — Software Development Plan

> **Document Type**: Software Requirements & Architecture Specification
> **Project**: Attendify – AI-Powered Attendance Management System
> **Version**: 1.2
> **Date**: 14 February 2026
> **Platform**: Android / iOS (React Native + Expo)
> **Stakeholders**: Student · Teacher · System Administrator

---

## 1. Executive Summary

Attendify is a cross-platform mobile application that automates institutional attendance management. The system offers **two distinct attendance mechanisms**:

| Mode | Description |
|:---|:---|
| **Manual** | Teacher-initiated roll-call via an in-app checklist |
| **AI-Automated** | Real-time face recognition from CCTV / classroom cameras that marks attendance without any human intervention |

The AI module operates as a **persistent background service**: when a student's face is detected and matched by the recognition model, the backend automatically inserts an attendance record — the student does not need to open the app or perform any action.

---

## 2. System Architecture

```mermaid
graph TB
    subgraph Client Layer
        SA["Student App<br/>(Expo / React Native)"]
        TA["Teacher App<br/>(Expo / React Native)"]
    end

    subgraph Backend Layer
        API["REST API Server<br/>(Python · FastAPI)"]
        AI["Face Recognition Engine<br/>(OpenCV · LBPH / dlib)"]
    end

    subgraph Infrastructure Layer
        DB["Supabase<br/>PostgreSQL Database"]
        ST["Supabase Storage<br/>student-faces bucket"]
        CAM["CCTV / IP Camera<br/>RTSP Stream"]
    end

    SA -- "HTTPS" --> API
    TA -- "HTTPS" --> API
    API -- "SQL" --> DB
    API -- "Upload / Download" --> ST
    CAM -- "RTSP / HTTP Stream" --> AI
    AI -- "Match Result" --> API
    API -- "INSERT attendance" --> DB
    AI -- "Fetch enrolled faces" --> ST
```

### Component Responsibilities

| Component | Role |
|:---|:---|
| **Student App** | Dashboard, attendance history, schedule view, face-photo enrollment, notifications |
| **Teacher App** | Manual attendance marking, AI monitoring dashboard, student management, schedule posting |
| **REST API (FastAPI)** | Central gateway — authenticates requests, serves data, receives recognition results, writes to DB |
| **Face Recognition Engine** | Captures frames from CCTV, runs face detection + matching against enrolled photos, sends match results to the API |
| **Supabase DB** | Persistent storage for profiles, classes, lectures, attendance records |
| **Supabase Storage** | Object store for student enrollment photos — organized by student ID |
| **CCTV / IP Camera** | Provides a live video stream (RTSP or HTTP) consumed by the recognition engine |

---

## 3. AI Attendance System — Connectivity & Flow

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The AI attendance system operates **fully automatically**. Once a student is visible in the classroom camera, the system detects and recognises their face, calls the backend API, and marks attendance — **without any manual action by the student or teacher**.

### 3.1 End-to-End Data Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant CAM as CCTV / IP Camera
    participant AI as Face Recognition Engine
    participant API as Backend API (FastAPI)
    participant DB as Supabase Database
    participant ST as Supabase Storage
    participant APP as Teacher App

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over CAM,ST: ① Continuous Frame Capture
        CAM->>AI: Stream video frames (RTSP / HTTP)
        AI->>AI: Detect faces using Haar Cascade / HOG
    end

    rect rgb(240, 255, 240)
        Note over AI,ST: ② Face Matching
        AI->>ST: Fetch enrolled face embeddings for active class
        ST-->>AI: Return stored embeddings / photos
        AI->>AI: Compare detected face vs enrolled faces (LBPH / dlib)
        AI->>AI: Confidence threshold check (≥ 70%)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 240)
        Note over AI,DB: ③ Automatic Attendance Logging
        AI->>API: POST /api/v1/attendance/recognise {student_id, lecture_id, confidence, frame_timestamp}
        API->>API: Validate request + deduplication check
        API->>DB: INSERT INTO attendance (student_id, lecture_id, status='Present', method='AI')
        DB-->>API: 201 Created
        API-->>AI: {success: true, attendance_id}
    end

    rect rgb(248, 240, 255)
        Note over API,APP: ④ Real-Time Notification
        API-->>APP: Push update to Teacher dashboard (WebSocket / Polling)
        APP-->>APP: Update live attendance feed
    end
```

### 3.2 Key Principles

| Principle | Implementation |
|:---|:---|
| **Zero Student Interaction** | Student only uploads photos once during enrollment. All subsequent attendance is marked automatically. |
| **Deduplication** | Backend rejects duplicate attendance for the same student + lecture. Only the first successful match is recorded. |
| **Confidence Threshold** | Matches below 70% confidence are logged as `uncertain` and flagged for teacher review — never auto-marked. |
| **Continuous Monitoring** | The recognition engine processes frames at ~2 FPS throughout the lecture duration. |
| **Teacher Override** | Teacher can manually correct any AI-marked record (change Present → Absent or vice-versa). |
| **Audit Trail** | Every AI-marked record stores `confidence_score` and `frame_timestamp` for accountability. |

