## 5. File Storage Architecture (Supabase Storage)

```
supabase-storage/
└── student-faces/                          ← Bucket (Public: No, RLS: Yes)
    ├── {student_uuid_1}/
    │   ├── photo_1.jpg                     ← Front-facing, well-lit
    │   ├── photo_2.jpg                     ← Slight left angle
    │   ├── photo_3.jpg                     ← Slight right angle
    │   ├── photo_4.jpg                     ← With glasses (optional)
    │   └── photo_5.jpg                     ← Different lighting
    ├── {student_uuid_2}/
    │   ├── photo_1.jpg
    │   ├── photo_2.jpg
    │   └── photo_3.jpg
    └── ...
```

### Storage Policies

| Policy | Rule |
|:---|:---|
| **Upload** | Only the authenticated student can upload to their own `/{student_id}/` path |
| **Read** | Backend service role can read any path (for recognition). Students can read only their own. |
| **Delete** | Students can delete their own photos. Teachers cannot modify student photos. |
| **File Format** | JPEG only, max 2 MB per image, minimum resolution 480×480 px |
| **Naming** | `photo_{index}.jpg` where index = 1–5 |
| **Compression** | Client-side compression to ≤ 500 KB before upload (using `expo-image-manipulator`) |

---

## 6. Database Schema (Supabase / PostgreSQL)

```mermaid
erDiagram
    profiles ||--o{ attendance : "has"
    profiles ||--o{ student_photos : "uploads"
    profiles ||--o{ lectures : "teaches"
    classes  ||--o{ lectures : "has"
    lectures ||--o{ attendance : "records"

    profiles {
        uuid id PK
        text full_name
        text email
        text roll_no
        text class
        text department
        text role "student | teacher"
        timestamptz created_at
    }
    classes {
        uuid id PK
        text name "e.g. CS-A Div 1"
        text department
        int student_count
    }
    lectures {
        uuid id PK
        uuid teacher_id FK
        uuid class_id FK
        text subject
        date lecture_date
        time start_time
        time end_time
        text room_no
    }
    attendance {
        uuid id PK
        uuid student_id FK
        uuid lecture_id FK
        text status "Present | Absent"
        text method "Manual | AI"
        float confidence_score "nullable - AI only"
        text camera_id "nullable - AI only"
        timestamptz marked_at
    }
    student_photos {
        uuid id PK
        uuid student_id FK
        text photo_url
        int photo_index "1 to 5"
        timestamptz uploaded_at
    }
```

